      "writtenOn": "2022-08-31T10:07:13Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Not sure if this is true, because it seems independent? Refer to:\nhttps://stackoverflow.com/questions/43055258/system-currenttimemillis-and-daylight-savings\nIf that is true, it should be fine whenever you want to format ctm into human readible format, right?\n\nBut general speaking, I would prefer to see the timestamp that matches the device log, that is easier to debug, even if it doesn\u0027t make sense. e.g.\n1. network connects at 2AM\n2. The user manually adjust system time to 1AM.\n3. 5 min later network disconnects, and a bug report is taken.\n\nI would prefer to see the network connects at 2:00, disconnects at 1:05 and total conneted time -55min in the log.\nBut what would the log say if the current solution is applied?",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 205,
        "startChar": 33,
        "endLine": 207,
        "endChar": 24
      },
      "revId": "bafffb92574b16ff310d8c154af4a0a418c3e0eb",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "a6031fb6_56d4336e",
        "filename": "service/src/com/android/server/connectivity/NetworkAgentInfo.java",
        "patchSetId": 3
      },
      "lineNbr": 207,
      "author": {
        "id": 1306837
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-08-31T12:12:20Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Rationale for current time millis is better:\n1. We don\u0027t really have a thing that is really rely on monotonic clock.\n2. The ctm-based timestamp might differ from the timstamp we see in the device log.  Which might make it harder to debug and clarify issue since they might not match if the user adjust system time multiple times.\n3. The use cases described were not a problem happened in pratice when we debug other modules. If it happens, we ask for clarifying the time change or just let the reporter reproduce again without touching the time.\n4. The conversion between a ctm-base timestamp and a real timestamp got from ctm is unknown to me. And I think people would be confused too.",
      "parentUuid": "bf4f3aa0_f960b2e0",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 205,
        "startChar": 33,
        "endLine": 207,
        "endChar": 24
      },
      "revId": "bafffb92574b16ff310d8c154af4a0a418c3e0eb",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "9eb71e6f_3b0196ab",
        "filename": "service/src/com/android/server/connectivity/NetworkAgentInfo.java",
        "patchSetId": 3
      },
      "lineNbr": 207,
      "author": {
        "id": 1015428
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-09-01T08:31:44Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Discussed within the team. Conclusions are :\n• A monotonic clock is important here. Debugging might go by with values that are occasionally wrong, but these timestamps are likely to be used in other ways in the code later, including for metrics in which outliers will be a problem.\n• To remove the confusion, never use System.currentTimeMillis(). Make all the timestamps based on elapsedRealTime(), and make sure dumpsys tells us the relationship so this can be reconstructed later when someone debugs.\n• If we find the abstruse numbers are difficult to manipulate when debugging, we can always improve their display later.\n\nImplemented according to the above.",
      "parentUuid": "a6031fb6_56d4336e",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 205,
        "startChar": 33,
        "endLine": 207,
        "endChar": 24
      },
      "revId": "bafffb92574b16ff310d8c154af4a0a418c3e0eb",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "47e49626_c646d28e",
        "filename": "service/src/com/android/server/connectivity/NetworkAgentInfo.java",
        "patchSetId": 3
      },
      "lineNbr": 207,
      "author": {
        "id": 1306837
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-09-01T09:32:17Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Ack.\nBut few thoughts for future reference:\n For metrics, IIUC what matters is the statistics in a large scale. For NTP adjustment or rarely adjust by user, I still don\u0027t think that would be a problem in pratice.\n For debugging, it seems to me consistency with the device log and convience for clarification is more importent to me. Consider people might miscalculate the real timestamp they need to check, and pass the analysis to next person, the overall total cost might be higher than we think.\n \n But we can see how it goes and modify the implementation if needed, so current plan is fine to me.",
      "parentUuid": "9eb71e6f_3b0196ab",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 205,
